{
  "id": "collection-challenge",
  "name": "Collection Challenge",
  "category": "campaign",
  "description": {
    "text": "The Collection Challenge (コレクションチャレンジ) was Pokémon Card Game's big campaign of summer 2008. From 10 July it handed out 13 original cards at cinemas showing the new Pokémon film, card and game shops, events and other places across Japan, a different Pokémon at each, with illustrations and attacks made for the campaign; Midori Harada drew eleven of the thirteen. Real World's Giratina went to the first 4 million viewers of Giratina and the Sky's Bouquet: Shaymin from 19 July, and Croagunk came with the film's souvenir program. Regigigas came from shops' launch campaign for the Intense Fight in the Destroyed Sky expansion, Pichu, Buneary and Lopunny from Trade Please DP swaps, Pikachu from a Pokémon Platinum quiz rally, Raichu for buying a Pokémon video game, Turtwig for finishing a railway stamp rally, Chimchar with children's clothes from Uniqlo, Piplup from Pokémon Challenge Hiroba events, Buizel from Gym Challenge shops and Pachirisu with issue 4 of Shogakukan's Pokémon Fan magazine.\n\nThe cards play together. Pichu, Pikachu and Raichu, and Buneary and Lopunny, each have an attack that grows stronger if it evolved from the one before that turn, and Turtwig, Chimchar, Piplup, Buizel, Pachirisu and Croagunk form a ring, each stronger when the next is in play. Members of the free Pokémon Daisuki Club could also collect the cards in a mini-game on its website until 1 September 2008; 300 of those who collected nine won, by draw, a set of the twelve given out at shops and events, all but Real World's Giratina.",
